[I] OBS Studio filter for applying an arbitrary shader to a source

[T] The obs-shaderfilter plugin for OBS Studio is intended to allow users to
[T] apply their own shaders to OBS sources. This theoretically makes possible
[T] some simple effects like drop shadows that can be implemented strictly in
[T] shader code.

[U] https://github.com/exeldro/obs-shaderfilter/

[A] Exeldro
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/multimedia
[F] CROSS OBJDIR

[L] GPL
[V] 2.6.1

[D] 840aa9f1b1a85d0dfbbc1293ea8b6e9f088f9ece5a9b070cdd393883 obs-shaderfilter-2.6.1.tar.gz https://github.com/exeldro/obs-shaderfilter/archive/refs/tags/2.6.1/

var_append cmakeopt ' ' "-DLIB_OUT_DIR=/${libdir##*/}/obs-plugins -DLINUX_PORTABLE=OFF"
